  "text": "Dubai registered 13,717 residential sales valued at AED 40.78bn in the last four weeks, representing a 34.5% increase in volume and a 47.4% rise in value compared to the previous period. Mortgage registrations totaled 5,775, which are recorded separately from sales. The top trading areas by twelve-week volume include Dubai South with 3,504 sales and Jumeirah Village Circle with 2,433 sales. Leading individual projects include Binghatti Skyterraces in Al Hebiah First with 619 sales and RAW DISTRICT 2 BY IMTIAZ in Down Town Jabal Ali with 589 sales.\n\nThe median residential price per square foot reached AED 1,741, up 4.5% from the prior four-week median of AED 1,666. Off-plan transactions accounted for 57.6% of total sales volume. In the rental sector, 92,075 Ejari contracts were registered with a renewal share of 51.8%. The median annual residential rent stood at AED 69,479.\n\nPrice momentum varies significantly across communities. Al Yufrah 1 showed the strongest heating with a 43.7% twelve-week increase in median price per square foot, followed by Dubai Industrial City at 12.9%. Conversely, Jumeirah Lakes Towers cooled by 14.6% and Palm Jumeirah by 14.3% over the same period. Estimated gross yields remain highest in Zaabeel First at 9.2% for flats, followed by International City Ph 1 at 8.6%.\n\nInvestors should monitor the 935 residential sales in the last 60 days that deviated more than 35% from their comparable cell median. These figures are derived from registered DLD data and Ejari contracts using medians and benchmark filters that exclude bulk deals, partial shares, mortgages, gifts, and statistical outliers.",
